WEBVTT

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:06.590
Your sins?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.420
It's about the previous
inspectors' accident.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.170
Please tell me.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:17.010
Before I became an enforcer,
I was a swimming athlete.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.850
I had a boyfriend back then.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.480
I've seen your record.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.690
It said that the two of you
were in a car crash.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.440
It wasn't our fault.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:33.320
Both of our Hues deteriorated
and we were institutionalized.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.450
But there was no change
in the perpetrator's Psycho-Pass.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.450
They got off with a fine.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:44.120
Later, my boyfriend
died in the institution.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.710
I was found suitable to be an enforcer
and accepted the post.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:53.050
I think I wanted an outlet for my anger.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.680
Draw the knives
locked behind your eyelids.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:03.390
Reap the lives that grow into shackles.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.190
Even the lost memories that flee
once they're liberated and banished

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:10.070
Are an everlasting cubism.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:31.040
Cause I know that in a future gone mad,

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.720
Even nightmares are peaceful.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.720
RESET, RESET, yeah.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.720
The midnight sun
awakens and turns to a riot.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:45.270
A gun for a faux-friendly kiss.
A knife for a faux-revolutionary hug.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:51.570
Get rid of it all, even the frozen chains.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:55.570
Reality is always outside your head.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:02:00.240
In a world seen through bestial eyes,

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:06.120
There is neither darkness nor light.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.920
Draw the knives
locked behind your eyelids.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.550
Reap the lives that grow into shackles.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.260
Even the false memories that flash before
your eyes impatiently and impulsively

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.890
Are an everlasting cubism.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.810
One day, a year ago,

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.980
I found online counseling.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.650
Chat with a Counselor

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.150
Open up and keep your Psycho-Pass clear.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:42.990
I was skeptical, but I still revealed
my frustration and desire for revenge.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:44.910
And then?

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:48.040
The same driver caused another accident.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:55.000
After a while,
that network sent me instructions

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:59.170
to file an investigation request
with their maintenance team.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:00.970
File a request?

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.470
"Our official vehicle's engine
sounds strange."

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.850
A false report.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.020
Then immediately afterwards,
the two previous inspectors...

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.730
I was one of the cogs in the machine.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:22.610
I got scared, and I've ignored
all instructions since then.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:27.540
Then, I started getting flowers

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.870
sent in my late boyfriend's name.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.500
A threat?

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:33.460
Yes.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:39.550
I realized they were sent by the man we
encountered at the Heaven's Leap facility.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.090
Koichi Azusawa?

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:46.390
He was manipulating me.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.600
What about the original driver?

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.350
They were temporarily quarantined,

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.730
but their Hue recovered
and now they live a normal life.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.190
How do you feel now?

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.860
It could have easily
turned out much worse.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.540
I'm prepared to accept the consequences.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.670
I'll speak to the chief.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.090
Don't tell anyone else yet.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.810
It's running a lot better.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:33.690
No matter how old it gets,
maintenance can bring it back.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:35.690
Just like counseling!

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:40.110
Psychological care and tinkering
with cars do have a lot in common.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.740
With time and effort, a mind can clear,

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:47.450
or be intentionally broken.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:55.080
It's been a long time, Inspector Shindo.

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:58.540
Akira. I'm glad you came.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.130
Kei.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.920
Arata, go play with Kei.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:04.340
OK.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.220
Come on, Kei.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:10.010
Go on.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.450
I'm going home.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.330
What am I,

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:36.370
Dad?

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.760
He's criminally asymptomatic.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:47.840
Akane Tsunemori must have known that.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:53.140
She made Shindo an inspector
because of some deal.

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:56.100
Setting speculations aside,

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:59.900
if his inspector suitability falls
below regulation,

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.980
he will be dealt with
as per protocol.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:04.110
No objections, I presume?

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:05.940
No, ma'am.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.780
The problem is Bifrost.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:12.580
My thought is

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:17.660
that it would have to predate
the Sibyl System in order to function.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:20.170
You think that's possible?

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:22.130
It's a hypothesis.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:24.590
I'll investigate and report on it.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:31.140
You are a capable and ideal citizen.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:34.560
I know that I'm really quite dull.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:39.390
Recently, not necessarily.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.320
You endorsed a real troublemaker!

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:46.030
But isn't he capable?

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.570
Those remnants showed up, too.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:51.240
You're going around
wrecking everything,

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:53.700
and I'm the one taking the fall for it!

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:56.490
You make it sound like I did it alone.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:07:01.290
Anyway,
I'll look after our two new inspectors.

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.210
You mean...

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:07.590
The CID is short-handed!

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.640
We can't afford to lose Shindo now.

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:18.020
You want to interview the CID?

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.940
Yes. For a documentary on justice.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:25.440
Don't you feel that justice in Japan
has changed?

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.650
Human justice has no value.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:34.990
Is that wrong for a member
of the Public Safety Bureau to say?

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:38.080
What is justice to you, Mika?

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:43.120
Doubt not God, test not God.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.630
Sibyl's justice and values
are beyond consideration.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:49.050
Then...

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:51.170
I didn't say no.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:54.300
Anything for you, Yayoi.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:56.470
Thank you.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:02.850
But couldn't you tell me more
about what you're really after?

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:07.820
This is for Akane, isn't it?

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.530
It's not that simple.

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.120
You're old friends and in the same unit.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.880
Do you think your superiors planned that?

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:28.340
"Planned"...?

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:33.130
We weren't chosen as a pair.
We just both happened to be qualified.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:37.510
Arata... Well, he does his best.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.180
Speak for yourself.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:40.640
That was a compliment.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:47.150
We conjecture Bifrost is an entity that
exploits the Sibyl System's blind spots.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:50.900
Their Crime Coefficients
may not even be measurable.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:54.400
But we know it has
a three-tiered structure.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:57.910
I've heard them mention "congressmen"

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.700
and also "inspectors."

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:05.330
Congressmen are the leaders
and inspectors are their subordinates.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:11.340
Foxes are the lowest level. Civilians
who don't know what they're doing.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:16.930
Because they're unaware,
their Crime Coefficients don't increase.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:20.350
A person who unknowingly
makes parts for a gun

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:23.850
and the person who fires it
have different Psycho-Passes.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.640
Why can't we locate them?

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:29.230
As for Koichi Azusawa,

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:33.650
his history and lifestyle are so random
that we can't track him down.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:37.820
He probably lives under someone else's ID.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.820
Is that even possible?

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:43.870
Practically speaking,
we have to assume so.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:47.210
I'm getting the picture.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:52.250
Something has gone wrong with
the blind spot they're hiding in.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:58.800
People living in safety only take risks
when that safety is threatened.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:03.390
Which means they'll target
the governor again.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.560
How can you be sure?

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:07.770
They're not indiscriminate.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:11.110
They targeted her
because they needed her dead.

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:14.570
You mean they're still
aiming for recovery?

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:16.650
That's right.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.080
How do I feel about my cases?

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:26.620
Seeing people die is really tough.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:30.130
Even under the Sibyl System,
unfortunate cases exist.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:34.460
There are always criminals
like those involved in this case.

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:37.300
What do you mean?

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:40.430
People who live to harm others.

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:42.100
There can't be many.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:44.100
Most are normal, right?

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:50.190
We've confirmed heavily armed criminals
separate from Bifrost.

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:52.810
Peacebreaker remnants?

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:54.440
Yeah, that's right.

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:57.150
They call themselves "Pathfinders" now.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:00.280
That's a problem.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.950
Um, what's "Peacebreaker"?

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:08.410
I authorize you to view level 3
classified materials. Look it up later.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:10.540
To put it simply,

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:15.500
it's a special forces unit involved
in the black market and overseas looting.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:19.420
It's one of the reasons
the current SAD was formed.

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:26.220
I want you to leave them to us.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.560
It doesn't feel like it's been lived in.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:35.020
It's too big for one person.

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:40.650
My father also served in the Ministry.

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:46.530
It's not like that's why I became
an inspector or anything, though.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.040
Foxes in the CID?

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:52.870
That's baseless.

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.590
Unit One is tightly knit.

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.420
You trust your colleagues, I see.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:00.970
Yes, of course I do.

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:06.260
Then why do you always hide
your real feelings?

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:11.310
There's a fox in the CID.

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:13.900
We have intel to that effect.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.400
I have the report.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:18.860
She fell into a trap.
She didn't betray us.

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:22.280
She'll even help us find Koichi Azusawa.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.030
Is it safe to trust her?

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:27.620
Public Safety will bear
the responsibility.

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:30.870
No, I trusted her.
The responsibility is mine.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:35.420
You can't take it all on yourself, Kei.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.250
It's my job. I'll do it.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:38.630
What's with you?

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.840
Hey, don't fight over it.

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:43.760
We'll take her off the scene
if issues arise.

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:48.550
Then we'll handle Peacebreaker.
You guard the governor.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:50.930
We'll also take Koichi Azusawa.

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:53.560
What?! In your dreams!

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:57.020
In that case,
the early bird catches the worm.

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:00.270
Fine by me.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:02.940
Until next time.

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:11.540
That's the extent of Kisaragi's
involvement with the foxes.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:15.540
And she's not responsible
for the accident?

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:19.000
She's not.
It'd be impossible to prove, anyway.

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:23.920
Well, at least she said something
before things got really bad.

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:28.970
But she'll be dead in the water
if she doesn't speak up sooner next time.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:31.510
I'm sorry.

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:37.650
Anyway, now we can start our fox hunt.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:42.190
We'll secure Governor Komiya
and lay a trap for Koichi Azusawa.

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:44.190
Meaning?

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:48.490
Kisaragi will contact Azusawa
and lure him out.

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:51.990
You're going to make Kisaragi act as bait?

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:54.250
Yes. We have to fool him.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:56.620
You'll make her confront him in person?

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:59.960
Any half-measures taken
against a mastermind will backfire.

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:03.340
So your plan's airtight, then?!

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:07.340
That's enough!

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:10.260
Enforcer Kisaragi will contact Azusawa.

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:14.270
Take no further dangerous action.
Dismissed.

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:20.020
There could still be foxes
in the Public Safety Bureau.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:22.270
Are they fighting?

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:25.360
It's about Inspector Ignatov's wife.

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:34.370
You almost never ask me to meet you.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:38.710
What's this?

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:41.830
The data I've gathered on your behavior.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:45.920
It's the original.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.220
You can destroy it.

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:51.140
So, you suspected me?

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:55.140
My role is to protect Unit One.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:56.890
That's why.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:02.060
That's my role, too.

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:08.570
Yes, I was glad when Sibyl chose me.

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:12.160
I was able to use my skills for peace

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:15.410
and to feel that I was a good person.

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:19.790
Justice?

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:23.000
It must be upheld.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:28.010
That's why I live without self-deception.

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:31.430
National Center for Medical Research

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.260
Her release was canceled?

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:36.140
Metropolitan policy? What is all this?

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:45.770
We're here to discuss a violent act by an
immigrant Public Safety Bureau inspector.

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:49.490
During the gubernatorial election,
this inspector

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:54.450
struck a supporter of Candidate Yakushiji,
causing his Hue to deteriorate.

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:59.080
Yes. He punched me for no reason at all.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:02.460
To be honest,
I thought he was going to kill me.

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:08.590
A rise in immigrant violence
has been my worst fear.

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:14.390
My government will take strong measures
to halt the spread of Hue deterioration.

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:18.470
We also have testimony that,
during the transport drone crash,

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:23.350
the inspector in question
threatened people with a Dominator.

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:34.160
This came in handy.

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:38.120
You can have it. It was Torri's, anyway.

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:42.750
Useful even after death.
No wonder he was loved by God.

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:46.750
Why can't you let an AI
handle this crap?

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:52.300
A little false reporting is all it takes
to get this bogus story trending.

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:55.800
You're talkative today. All fired up?

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:59.310
I got promoted to Eleven, thanks to you.

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:01.930
We'll have to celebrate.

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:03.850
How about I kill you, scumbag?

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:07.190
Hey, what's that?

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:09.020
A banned book.

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:13.530
Hoffmann's
"The Nutcracker and the Mouse King."

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:14.860
Is it any good?

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:17.780
I like the fight scenes.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:21.580
The nutcracker is a soldier
who battles evil mice.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:25.710
To rescue a princess,
made hideous by magic,

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:29.670
he needs to crack the world's hardest nut,
Crackatook.

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:34.050
What do you think Crackatook
is a metaphor for?

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:37.840
Your balls.

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:41.310
You're the best, Obata.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:43.770
I love you. Seriously.

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:46.390
Shut up.

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:50.730
Right now, the Public Safety Bureau
is my Crackatook.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:55.570
Especially Shindo. He's Atsushi's son.

00:17:56.360 --> 00:18:00.070
I've got to crack him
before he becomes like his father.

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:13.420
I am Karina Komiya, Governor of Tokyo.

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:15.010
Yes, we've met.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:20.550
Welcome to Public Safety, Governor Komiya.

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:23.180
Thank you for taking our request.

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:26.270
I'll be in your care for a little while.

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:28.230
Please wait.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:30.770
And you are?

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:33.270
Vice-Governor Mitsumori.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:36.110
I oversee immigrant policy.

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:37.530
I see...

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:41.570
I ask you to refrain from assigning
immigrants to her detail.

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:46.290
Isn't he the one who was on the news?

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.790
His wife is a latent criminal.

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:50.920
She is not a latent criminal!

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:53.540
You just won't let her be released!

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:59.970
You should know this is a difficult
time due to immigrant-related incidents.

00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:05.560
You need to realize that your attitude
will only make matters worse.

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:06.970
What was that?!

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:08.480
Stop, Kei.

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:10.310
Are you on her side?!

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:12.810
Stop this, Inspector Ignatov.

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:14.940
Stand by.

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:16.650
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:22.450
Yes, I was irritated at being removed
from the security detail,

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:25.910
but it worked out for the best.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:29.120
Now I can focus on the hunt.

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:35.290
I can't ignore the governor's requests.

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:38.420
So, a political decision, huh?

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:42.220
You just gotta swallow this pill,
Inspector Ignatov.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:45.470
I want you
to remove Enforcer Todoroki as well.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:48.680
What?! How can I go along with that?

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:53.600
Inspector Ignatov, Todoroki, and Kisaragi
will handle the fox hunt.

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:58.820
Inspector Shindo, Irie, and Hinakawa
will protect the governor. Understood?

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:01.610
Yes, ma'am.

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:06.370
Can't Inspector Shindo protect
the governor on his own?

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:09.200
The governor dislikes enforcers.

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.370
Isn't that what the enemy wants?

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:16.290
They could use bias against immigrants
and latent criminals to isolate her.

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:21.380
Why don't you control the people who think
politics means spreading discrimination?

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:24.390
Isn't manipulation your specialty?!

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:29.770
Personnel only. No admittance.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:35.650
I'm grateful to the inspector
for hitting my brother.

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:40.730
All of us here are hopelessly human.

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:44.950
We can't control our anger,
and we say sorry if something goes wrong.

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:48.370
Sibyl wouldn't approve,
but it's a perk of this place.

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:51.620
I'm sure you understand.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.080
Justice?

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:58.250
I'm not sure.

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:02.920
I mean, it's kind of
an embarrassing word to say,

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:06.050
but those who use it in earnest,
really shine.

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:14.890
How much can mental tracing
control someone?

00:21:15.020 --> 00:21:17.650
It's more effective than some counseling.

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:21.650
It's called psychic driving.

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:23.650
What about your father?

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:27.990
Kei... are you...?

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:36.000
I don't know what you're thinking, but...

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:40.250
Have you ever "driven" me or Maiko?

00:21:42.590 --> 00:21:45.970
No. I haven't. I would never.

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:50.720
I've never done it for myself.

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:55.060
Mentalist, heal thyself.

00:22:02.270 --> 00:22:05.070
I've heard your songs.

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:06.900
They're all pretty good.

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:08.450
Thank you.

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:14.660
I'd like to hear what you think of
an idol-politician like Karina Komiya.

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:19.580
The people and Sibyl wanted her.
Nothing more, nothing less.

00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:24.340
The old you would have recorded
a bunch of dis tracks against her.

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:28.590
Hey, don't forget
that you're the one being interviewed.

00:22:31.850 --> 00:22:33.180
Justice, huh?

00:22:34.310 --> 00:22:36.850
It's a word losers shout a lot.

00:22:38.230 --> 00:22:42.310
My dad died believing in that word.

00:22:45.570 --> 00:22:50.660
This may be indiscreet of me,
but I guess I'm glad to see you again.

00:22:51.990 --> 00:22:54.910
I feel a little bit better
to hear you say so.

00:22:55.790 --> 00:22:59.580
I'm sorry about your partner.
It's my fault.

00:23:00.210 --> 00:23:02.540
That's not entirely true.

00:23:03.290 --> 00:23:05.050
Are you scared of something?

00:23:05.920 --> 00:23:07.380
What do you mean?

00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:09.720
You used to be more carefree.

00:23:10.260 --> 00:23:11.760
I'm a bit busy.

00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:14.560
By the way, where's your first secretary?

00:23:15.140 --> 00:23:17.850
I laid En off.

00:23:18.770 --> 00:23:19.480
What?

00:23:19.600 --> 00:23:20.890
Party policy.

00:23:21.270 --> 00:23:24.730
I couldn't keep En at my side,
all because of that.

00:23:25.610 --> 00:23:27.230
Just like your partner.

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:34.660
Politics is the one way to reduce violence
and minimize conflict.

00:23:36.410 --> 00:23:38.080
That's why I'm a politician.

00:23:39.370 --> 00:23:42.830
I'll make this a country
where no one can complain

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:48.420
even if En or your partner
were at my side.

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:51.180
That's admirable.

00:23:51.300 --> 00:23:52.720
What's gotten into you?

00:23:53.470 --> 00:23:56.060
I can understand your position
and beliefs.

00:23:56.640 --> 00:23:58.270
And I have a request.

00:23:59.350 --> 00:24:01.850
Please release my partner's wife.

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:04.400
I'll do what I can.

00:24:04.980 --> 00:24:07.900
In exchange, make sure you keep me safe.

00:24:09.280 --> 00:24:12.910
Mao's fake security schedule
is on the Public Safety Bureau

00:24:13.030 --> 00:24:16.120
and Metropolitan Policy Bureau servers.

00:24:16.370 --> 00:24:19.370
Then the enemy will see
how convenient Kisaragi is.

00:24:19.910 --> 00:24:21.290
Will they notice?

00:24:22.670 --> 00:24:24.580
Let's trust the enemy's competence.

00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:33.010
I owe my life to Inspector Ignatov
and his wife.

00:24:33.680 --> 00:24:37.640
The inspector is a strong-willed person,
worthy of respect.

00:24:38.810 --> 00:24:41.180
You seem like a strong person yourself.

00:24:41.930 --> 00:24:42.810
I'm not.

00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:47.520
Every time a crime occurs,
I'm reminded of how weak I am.

00:24:48.860 --> 00:24:50.940
Risking our lives to protect others.

00:24:51.280 --> 00:24:55.610
I've realized recently
that that's what justice means for us.

00:24:59.080 --> 00:25:02.040
Enforcer Kisaragi Mao

00:25:08.340 --> 00:25:09.000
It's here.

00:25:13.340 --> 00:25:15.930
I guess that's about it for the case.

00:25:16.470 --> 00:25:18.930
Should you really tell all this
to an outsider?

00:25:20.010 --> 00:25:24.180
I know you know what's safe to air
and what isn't.

00:25:26.850 --> 00:25:31.690
My Crime Coefficient
has been dropping lately, too.

00:25:32.820 --> 00:25:35.240
I thought I'd spend my whole life here.

00:25:36.450 --> 00:25:37.910
Ever heard this story?

00:25:38.070 --> 00:25:42.450
A species of lizard was chased
into the trees by an invasive species.

00:25:43.250 --> 00:25:48.420
After 15 years, the lizards' bodies
had adapted to cling to trees,

00:25:49.920 --> 00:25:52.380
and they couldn't go back to the ground.

00:25:53.710 --> 00:25:55.380
You're not a lizard.

00:26:00.140 --> 00:26:03.600
You've always wanted to be a congressman,
haven't you?

00:26:03.930 --> 00:26:06.270
Due to my unfortunate upbringing.

00:26:06.560 --> 00:26:08.940
It was a tragic drama...

00:26:09.940 --> 00:26:12.230
That's not the story I know.

00:26:12.610 --> 00:26:15.990
Nothing gets past you.
I don't remember my childhood.

00:26:16.740 --> 00:26:19.660
My trauma comes from
my Ministry of Welfare days.

00:26:20.030 --> 00:26:21.910
Atsushi Shindo?

00:26:22.080 --> 00:26:23.080
Yes.

00:26:23.290 --> 00:26:26.830
Being crushed by him awakened my talents.

00:26:27.410 --> 00:26:32.340
I hate him,
but he was also my greatest teacher.

00:26:32.800 --> 00:26:34.170
Interesting.

00:26:34.300 --> 00:26:38.510
To be frank, a man of your ability
is worthy of being a congressman.

00:26:38.840 --> 00:26:40.260
Just what I wanted to hear!

00:26:40.390 --> 00:26:43.560
But there are those
who oppose your appointment.

00:26:45.560 --> 00:26:47.430
That makes it more worthwhile.

00:26:47.680 --> 00:26:49.940
There's also Shindo's son.

00:26:50.940 --> 00:26:54.070
Arata Shindo is criminally asymptomatic.

00:26:54.320 --> 00:26:57.030
He was born immune to Sibyl's judgment.

00:26:57.490 --> 00:27:00.070
A being equal to Bifrost.

00:27:00.530 --> 00:27:04.030
What does it mean
to be "criminally asymptomatic"?

00:27:05.450 --> 00:27:08.540
You'll find out
when you become a congressman.

00:27:14.380 --> 00:27:16.510
Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building

00:27:23.430 --> 00:27:27.020
I'll check the parking lot, Inspector.
Please stand by.

00:27:27.220 --> 00:27:28.100
Understood.

00:27:29.940 --> 00:27:34.360
There sure are a lot
of paparazzi drones out.

00:27:35.230 --> 00:27:37.480
There have been a lot of cases lately.

00:27:38.360 --> 00:27:41.990
And everyone is oversensitive
when it comes to immigrants.

00:27:45.160 --> 00:27:46.160
Shion.

00:27:46.330 --> 00:27:47.830
Yes? What is it?

00:27:48.450 --> 00:27:52.370
Please track all nearby drones
and send me the data.

00:27:52.830 --> 00:27:54.170
Let me see...

00:27:54.630 --> 00:27:56.550
Hey, that's too many of them!

00:27:56.710 --> 00:27:58.710
As fast as possible, please.

00:28:01.380 --> 00:28:02.510
What was that about?

00:28:03.220 --> 00:28:06.930
If they set a trap,
they'll put surveillance support in place.

00:28:07.180 --> 00:28:08.430
That's what I'd do.

00:28:08.810 --> 00:28:10.180
What you would do?

00:28:11.060 --> 00:28:14.230
Do you and the criminal
think so much alike?

00:28:14.560 --> 00:28:15.560
Of course not.

00:28:16.060 --> 00:28:19.690
His disinterest in humans makes me sick.

00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:22.320
He sees a world full of people

00:28:22.700 --> 00:28:25.410
as nothing but a gigantic puzzle.

00:28:26.490 --> 00:28:28.990
He treats people as game pieces.

00:28:29.410 --> 00:28:32.370
People who make the wrong choices
die on their own.

00:28:33.170 --> 00:28:35.040
His contrivances assure that.

00:28:35.880 --> 00:28:38.880
But you can figure them out, can't you?

00:28:40.760 --> 00:28:41.970
Barely.

00:28:43.760 --> 00:28:46.850
This is an investigation, isn't it?

00:28:47.220 --> 00:28:52.430
I mean, you're the only former member
of Unit One with freedom of movement.

00:28:54.600 --> 00:28:59.070
Everything I know about justice,
I learned in CID Unit One

00:29:00.070 --> 00:29:03.240
from Inspector Tsunemori.

00:29:11.290 --> 00:29:13.750
I'll go alone
so they don't suspect anything.

00:29:14.580 --> 00:29:16.830
Without backup? I can't agree to that.

00:29:17.420 --> 00:29:18.920
I'm against it as well.

00:29:19.250 --> 00:29:22.340
Besides,
this used to be Enomiya's headquarters.

00:29:22.880 --> 00:29:26.550
Don't worry.
I'll contact you when I need backup.

00:29:30.680 --> 00:29:32.060
What's this about?

00:29:33.230 --> 00:29:36.060
It's about Congressman Shirogane.

00:29:36.480 --> 00:29:38.940
He wants to eliminate you.

00:29:39.400 --> 00:29:40.270
And?

00:29:40.980 --> 00:29:42.610
He plans to use me.

00:29:44.030 --> 00:29:45.700
That sounds like Shirogane.

00:29:46.660 --> 00:29:50.370
You're weighing him and me
against each other, I suppose?

00:29:50.910 --> 00:29:54.370
No. I want to help you.

00:29:54.750 --> 00:29:56.580
You're like me.

00:29:56.710 --> 00:29:58.290
That's a misunderstanding.

00:29:58.500 --> 00:29:59.170
Oh?

00:30:00.290 --> 00:30:02.590
Why do you want to be a congressman?

00:30:03.340 --> 00:30:04.800
It's no use dissembling.

00:30:05.470 --> 00:30:09.640
As long as people live,
they are merely cogs in society's machine.

00:30:09.760 --> 00:30:12.760
In which case, I want to be on top.

00:30:13.970 --> 00:30:16.640
I'm glad you answered honestly.

00:30:16.940 --> 00:30:21.820
In the sense that we do not place value
on people's humanity,

00:30:22.110 --> 00:30:24.150
we are indeed alike.

00:30:24.320 --> 00:30:24.940
Then...?

00:30:25.070 --> 00:30:28.820
But I don't think of people as cogs.

00:30:29.030 --> 00:30:31.200
And I despise games.

00:30:32.080 --> 00:30:33.990
But you're so good at them.

00:30:34.540 --> 00:30:37.040
Preferences have nothing to do with that.

00:30:37.580 --> 00:30:39.500
I knew I liked you.

00:30:40.040 --> 00:30:45.170
I'll show you proof that you need me.
Wait a moment.

00:31:10.070 --> 00:31:12.950
You're the fox messenger?
I want further instructions.

00:31:15.240 --> 00:31:17.370
I knew this was a setup.

00:31:18.160 --> 00:31:21.750
Yes, I knew he was the most dangerous.

00:31:25.340 --> 00:31:27.960
Public Safety Inspector Ignatov,
I presume?

00:31:29.010 --> 00:31:29.880
What?

00:31:31.130 --> 00:31:32.760
I'll be brief.

00:31:33.300 --> 00:31:37.270
I am involved with Bifrost
in an important capacity.

00:31:39.100 --> 00:31:40.890
You're not a fox?

00:31:41.140 --> 00:31:42.020
No.

00:31:42.150 --> 00:31:46.230
And, for certain reasons,
my life is currently in danger.

00:31:46.650 --> 00:31:47.730
What do you mean?

00:31:49.900 --> 00:31:53.240
Enomiya was a monomaniac.

00:31:55.200 --> 00:31:57.120
I'm sure they made escape routes.

00:31:59.080 --> 00:32:01.710
They'll probably send
the two Pathfinders.

00:32:02.120 --> 00:32:04.630
We can't beat them in a fair fight.

00:32:28.730 --> 00:32:29.440
Gino!

00:32:40.580 --> 00:32:43.460
I want you to protect me. However,

00:32:44.500 --> 00:32:47.960
promise that you will not mention me
to anyone.

00:32:48.170 --> 00:32:50.090
What are you babbling about?

00:32:50.420 --> 00:32:53.470
In exchange, I will release your wife.

00:32:55.430 --> 00:32:56.470
What do you mean?

00:33:02.520 --> 00:33:03.190
Here.

00:33:04.940 --> 00:33:05.900
Take this.

00:33:12.690 --> 00:33:15.200
If you want to learn the truth from me,

00:33:16.070 --> 00:33:19.280
register your biometrics with the device.

00:33:44.520 --> 00:33:48.730
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs?
Don't let them come in contact with me.

00:33:49.110 --> 00:33:52.530
Help me escape from here on your own.

00:33:52.690 --> 00:33:53.530
Who are you?

00:33:53.650 --> 00:33:54.360
No time.

00:33:55.070 --> 00:33:58.870
Choose.
Cooperate with me or abandon me.

00:34:01.240 --> 00:34:02.120
Follow me.

00:34:16.170 --> 00:34:17.220
Time's up.

00:34:22.060 --> 00:34:24.220
We'll kill you next time.

00:34:30.480 --> 00:34:32.570
Sorry. They got away.

00:34:33.230 --> 00:34:35.070
Both enemies were present?

00:34:35.190 --> 00:34:36.400
I confirmed it.

00:34:36.860 --> 00:34:39.240
There's no doubt. It's them.

00:34:41.030 --> 00:34:42.490
You all right, Kogami?

00:34:42.620 --> 00:34:45.370
Yeah. More importantly,

00:34:47.210 --> 00:34:48.750
something bothers me.

00:34:49.500 --> 00:34:52.340
Fast work. That's our Shion.

00:34:52.460 --> 00:34:55.090
There are an awful lot of drones.

00:34:55.880 --> 00:34:57.510
How do we find the right one?

00:35:03.510 --> 00:35:08.100
Crackers can't help but leave a signature.

00:35:30.620 --> 00:35:32.130
We're with Public Safety.

00:35:32.750 --> 00:35:33.630
What?

00:35:34.500 --> 00:35:35.880
Please come with us.

00:35:37.590 --> 00:35:40.090
Crime Coefficient is under 60.

00:35:40.380 --> 00:35:42.300
Not a target for enforcement action.

00:35:42.510 --> 00:35:44.470
The trigger will be locked.

00:35:45.010 --> 00:35:46.640
She's clean, Inspector.

00:35:46.930 --> 00:35:48.180
It doesn't matter.

00:35:48.390 --> 00:35:49.810
Isn't that a bit...

00:35:50.440 --> 00:35:52.650
Is this compulsory?

00:35:53.440 --> 00:35:57.030
It can be.
Would you like me to get authorization?

00:35:58.360 --> 00:36:02.160
Shut up.
Fine, I'll go. Happy?

00:36:07.790 --> 00:36:09.450
That was good work.

00:36:13.380 --> 00:36:16.040
Are you a congressman?

00:36:16.670 --> 00:36:21.550
I'm someone who can give you
what you currently most desire.

00:36:22.180 --> 00:36:25.180
Now, make up your mind and choose.

00:36:46.910 --> 00:36:48.620
Are you OK? What happened?

00:36:49.620 --> 00:36:50.580
No problems.

00:36:51.250 --> 00:36:52.960
Sorry I didn't contact you.

00:37:00.590 --> 00:37:03.010
What happened in there? Answer me.

00:37:03.630 --> 00:37:06.050
I simply evacuated a civilian.

00:37:06.390 --> 00:37:08.430
More importantly, what about them?

00:37:09.430 --> 00:37:11.770
The Peacebreaker remnants fled.

00:37:12.390 --> 00:37:15.400
Then you're the ones
who let your target get away!

00:37:19.440 --> 00:37:22.280
You can't cover up a lie
forever, Inspector.

00:37:23.240 --> 00:37:26.030
Stop interfering in our jurisdiction.

00:37:26.700 --> 00:37:32.120
I'll file a formal complaint with
your chief for obstructing our operation.

00:37:35.580 --> 00:37:36.420
We're leaving.

00:37:43.510 --> 00:37:44.920
Aren't you late?

00:37:46.300 --> 00:37:47.510
I ran into trouble.

00:37:48.340 --> 00:37:50.720
How unfortunate.

00:37:53.020 --> 00:37:54.230
On with the game.

00:37:59.110 --> 00:38:00.690
You moron!

00:38:00.980 --> 00:38:05.070
What were you thinking,
acting without your enforcers?!

00:38:05.200 --> 00:38:07.110
That was too reckless, Kei.

00:38:07.240 --> 00:38:11.450
You too, idiot! What did you bring in
someone with a clear Hue for?!

00:38:12.120 --> 00:38:14.580
She came in for voluntary questioning.

00:38:14.830 --> 00:38:16.620
Under threat of a forced search?

00:38:17.120 --> 00:38:21.210
Oh, I give up! Get out, both of you!
I don't want to look at you!

00:38:21.840 --> 00:38:24.340
Wait, I need permission to question...

00:38:24.630 --> 00:38:25.470
Get out!

00:38:27.630 --> 00:38:28.510
How did it go?

00:38:29.140 --> 00:38:31.350
We caught a fox by the tail.

00:38:31.850 --> 00:38:35.390
Ms. Chiyo Obata. What a lovely name.

00:38:35.770 --> 00:38:38.980
So what?
You planning to make my Hue cloud?

00:38:39.520 --> 00:38:42.320
I'm both an inspector and a mentalist.

00:38:42.650 --> 00:38:45.650
I can manipulate you, but I won't.

00:38:46.240 --> 00:38:48.150
Your dad would've.

00:39:09.680 --> 00:39:10.930
Biometrics confirmed.

00:39:11.840 --> 00:39:14.180
Thirteenth Inspector registered.

00:39:14.510 --> 00:39:15.270
Kei Mikhail Ignatov

00:39:17.730 --> 00:39:20.400
Contract signed. Your wife will be
discharged tomorrow. I'll be in touch.

00:39:21.730 --> 00:39:22.860
Discharged?

00:39:26.610 --> 00:39:27.570
I'm home.

00:39:28.780 --> 00:39:29.740
Maiko!

00:39:32.280 --> 00:39:34.080
Did you get me out?

00:39:34.490 --> 00:39:35.950
I didn't do anything.

00:39:37.330 --> 00:39:39.370
This is only natural.

00:39:41.420 --> 00:39:42.960
Are your eyes all right?

00:39:43.250 --> 00:39:45.460
They say the surgery was a success.

00:39:46.630 --> 00:39:48.760
I'll be able to see once I settle down.

00:39:49.840 --> 00:39:53.090
I'll brew tea and make dinner.

00:39:53.600 --> 00:39:55.470
Let me. It's been so long.

00:39:56.390 --> 00:39:58.390
Let's cook together, then.

00:40:02.270 --> 00:40:05.610
You've made a series of blunders, First.

00:40:06.400 --> 00:40:09.900
Not at all.
They were all calculated opening moves.

00:40:10.240 --> 00:40:15.070
Was adding a new inspector part your plan
as well?

00:40:15.950 --> 00:40:19.450
Shizuka enlisted him as your rival.

00:40:20.460 --> 00:40:21.870
Well, now.

00:40:22.580 --> 00:40:24.580
Don't falter in the endgame.

00:40:25.590 --> 00:40:27.090
Don't worry.

00:40:31.670 --> 00:40:33.720
This is where the real game begins.

00:40:41.520 --> 00:40:43.270
Yeah. Not bad.

00:40:46.480 --> 00:40:49.780
Thank goodness
they let you out, Mai.

00:40:50.780 --> 00:40:53.150
Listen, I heard you had a fight with Kei.

00:40:53.320 --> 00:40:55.110
Oh, yeah...

00:40:55.450 --> 00:40:58.280
He's sorry for getting too angry.

00:40:58.660 --> 00:41:01.450
It was because I failed to protect you.

00:41:01.830 --> 00:41:04.290
What are you both afraid of?

00:41:06.460 --> 00:41:09.170
Are we afraid of something?

00:41:10.300 --> 00:41:13.380
Neither of you is prepared.

00:41:15.010 --> 00:41:16.680
You're strong, Mai.

00:41:17.350 --> 00:41:20.680
I'm not prepared to see this world,
either.

00:41:23.310 --> 00:41:25.350
But I'll be able to see it one day.

00:41:25.980 --> 00:41:29.020
After all,
it's not the world itself that scares us.

00:41:29.320 --> 00:41:32.070
It's the thought
of losing our bonds, right?

00:41:33.190 --> 00:41:35.990
Yeah. I think you're right.

00:41:36.360 --> 00:41:38.870
So, Kei hit you, right?

00:41:39.030 --> 00:41:40.700
You can hit him back, OK?

00:41:41.990 --> 00:41:43.120
Good idea.

00:41:43.660 --> 00:41:45.920
Then I'll apologize to Kei.

00:41:49.210 --> 00:41:50.550
Your girlfriend?

00:41:51.380 --> 00:41:52.210
No.

00:41:52.550 --> 00:41:54.050
My best friend's wife.

00:41:58.510 --> 00:41:59.640
Cologne?

00:42:00.050 --> 00:42:00.720
For me?

00:42:01.390 --> 00:42:06.020
Having a nice scent on hand when
you're busy is good for your Hue, right?

00:42:06.390 --> 00:42:07.480
Thank you.

00:42:07.850 --> 00:42:10.020
You take care of everything for me.

00:42:10.610 --> 00:42:12.730
I should be the one thanking you.

00:42:20.580 --> 00:42:21.780
You seem healthy.

00:42:22.120 --> 00:42:22.790
Yes.

00:42:23.580 --> 00:42:26.120
I've always been physically tough.

00:42:27.250 --> 00:42:28.880
Everyone's the same as ever.

00:42:29.670 --> 00:42:30.880
I see.

00:42:31.380 --> 00:42:33.550
Your conviction was right.

00:42:34.550 --> 00:42:36.880
You'll be able to say so proudly one day.

00:42:38.430 --> 00:42:41.640
Please tell me about yourself sometime,
too.

00:42:42.680 --> 00:42:46.730
Sure. I've got stories from my long trip.

00:42:59.160 --> 00:43:04.660
CID Unit One's current investigations
and the last case I was involved in

00:43:05.370 --> 00:43:07.830
are all connected. I'm sure of it.

00:43:09.710 --> 00:43:14.420
I honestly don't know
what justice means to me personally.

00:43:16.130 --> 00:43:19.430
But I can't control the truth.

00:43:20.640 --> 00:43:22.600
The control of justice...

00:43:44.910 --> 00:43:45.620
Dad,

00:43:48.000 --> 00:43:49.960
I won't run from the truth,

00:43:51.120 --> 00:43:53.630
so that I won't go wrong.

00:43:54.380 --> 00:43:55.380
Isn't that right,

00:43:57.170 --> 00:43:58.050
Kei?

00:44:14.690 --> 00:44:17.650
Stupid perfection in your own castle

00:44:19.860 --> 00:44:23.490
How smart. You cause me to yawn

00:44:24.910 --> 00:44:30.330
Look,
The key to the door is in your hand

00:44:30.540 --> 00:44:35.630
Don't you let anyone take control

00:44:35.750 --> 00:44:40.920
What do you want?

00:44:41.090 --> 00:44:46.300
Go get it. Play by your own rule

00:44:46.430 --> 00:44:52.180
The winner always controls the game

00:44:52.350 --> 00:44:57.190
You stand in your belief

00:45:00.570 --> 00:45:05.030
There's no promising future

00:45:05.530 --> 00:45:10.660
Always helpless
Crying for the moon

00:45:10.790 --> 00:45:15.880
Finger trembles in fear
With the weight of the trigger

00:45:16.080 --> 00:45:19.050
There's a way for us

00:45:19.250 --> 00:45:23.220
Show them how we fight

00:45:23.420 --> 00:45:26.390
Pull the trigger

00:45:42.740 --> 00:45:45.400
So long to the legendary lady detective.

00:45:47.030 --> 00:45:48.280
"Psycho-Pass" refers to the measurement
of a person's mind and personality.

00:45:48.450 --> 00:45:49.740
This is a work of fiction. Any resemblance
to real persons or groups is coincidental.
